  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. The difference with the hard version is highlighted in bold.**\n\nYou are given a tree containing NNN vertices and N−1N-1N−1 undirected edges. You have to color each vertex of the tree either red, blue, or green.\n\nEach vertex must receive exactly one color, and there should also be at least one vertex having each color in the end.\n\nFor a vertex uuu, define score(u)\\text{score}(u)score(u) to be the sum of distances from uuu, to the closest vertices of the other two colors.\n\nMore clearly, if uuu is colored red, let d1d_1d1​ be the minimum distance from uuu to a green vertex, and d2d_2d2​ be the minimum distance from uuu to a blue vertex.\nThen, we have\n\nscore(u)=d1+d2\\text{score}(u) = d_1 + d_2score(u)=d1​+d2​The distance between two vertices uuu and vvv is equal to the number of edges on the simple path between uuu and vvv in the tree.\n\nThe beauty of the tree is calculated as the sum of score(u)\\text{score}(u)score(u) across all vertices uuu.\n\n**Your task is to output the minimum possible beauty of the tree that can be achieved over all valid colorings.**\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of vertices in the tree.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an undirected edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case you have to output a single integer denoting the **minimum possible beauty** of the tree that can be achieved over all valid colorings, each on a new line.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The input edges describe a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
